    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296-a8">

                <pb facs="0353" n="1087" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1087"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 7 in No.
                    74.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Chichkine to Mr.
                            Breckinridge.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >St. Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-02-22"><hi rendition="#italic">February 22/March 6,
                            1895</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: In answer to my note of January
                    25/February 6, you have expressed the desire to receive information of a more
                    explicit nature in regard to the course of the case of John Ginzberg.</p>
                <p>You will not ignore that the purpose of the note mentioned by you was to reassure
                    you as to the humane treatment on the part of the imperial authorities; as
                    regards the case of Ginzberg, it is at the present time, as I had the honor to
                    inform you, in the hands of the justice and is following its course, and I
                    therefore can not give the desired explicit details before a corresponding
                    communication reaches me from our judicial authorities.</p>
                <p>Receive, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chichkine.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
